+
+## Agent form tools
+
+In browsers supporting declarative WebMCP, the sign-in and sign-up pages expose
+`sign-in` and `sign-up` tools respectively. Their named, required controls provide
+the username and password schema. Both tools use the same submission handlers and
+API requests as manual submissions and return success or error messages through
+`SubmitEvent.respondWith()`.
+
+These account forms omit `toolautosubmit`, retaining the browser's user review
+step. Browsers without WebMCP continue to use the forms normally.
